WEBVTT

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.590
Is the data accurate?

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.230
Yes... Although I don't know why.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.500
Ever since then, MESS has stopped

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.720
all harmful activity 
toward human society.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.400
Ohhh... Is this a reaction, too?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.040
Don't tell me! You love origami, too?

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.390
All the absorbed humans have 
been safely returned, as well.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.710
No way!

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.740
That's way too awesome!

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.340
Case closed!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.700
We can't let down our guard just yet!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.260
They just stopped <i>doing</i> anything;

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.050
they haven't stopped 
making an appearance.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.520
C'mon, can't you just 
be happy, Pai-Pai?

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.230
Don't call me Pai-Pai!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.080
Oh, do you prefer Pai-san, after all?

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.480
You're messing with me.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:54.000
So you're saying that no one's 
been abducted since then?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.820
Yes. No one since.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.990
Huh? What?

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.940
Not "What?"!

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.540
What'd you do to it back there?

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.240
I just thought I'd make it cute.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.210
Hey, doesn't it seem like it's 
communicating with Hajime-chan?

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.800
Oh, it's MESSY-chan.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.680
Why are you introducing it to us?!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.690
I mean, don't even name it!

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.010
There's no way anyone can 
communicate with a MESS...

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.870
Wh-What?

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.110
Its shape-changing might have 
something to do with this.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.240
Oh, we collaborated with our scissors.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.610
Oh, that must be it!

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.360
Change the body's shape 
to exchange information, maybe?

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.620
Maybe that's how 
they communicate.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.660
That's way too far-fetched!

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.180
But, it's strange.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.280
Why did all the MESS act 
as one, at the same time?

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.390
Maybe they can share information.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:53.630
What?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.980
So, just like with this NOTE,

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.260
information might be 
transmitted instantaneously.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.970
They might be a life 
form with a hive mind.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.950
That's kind of sexy!

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.280
How?!

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.260
Forget it!

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.510
My orders were to exterminate!

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.400
But when we try 
to catch it, it vanishes.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.730
That's impossible!

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.740
Aww, so cute!

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.970
Maybe MESS-chan never had any animosity 
toward us in the first place,

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.770
and just didn't realize 
we were around.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.170
Impossible!

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.860
Ouch...

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.590
They've clearly been doing 
harm until recently!

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:42.050
"Oh, no! I've stepped on an ant!"

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.230
Kind of like that?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.140
Even a philanthropist like me might 
do that while I'm walking about.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.570
You don't mean...

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.550
From their perspective, 
we're like ants?

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.770
Ants might be giving 
us a lot of credit.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.150
Might be more like rocks.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.530
Way too sad!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.120
I'm gloomy...

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.830
Th-Then, what we've been 
doing until now is...

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.500
A waste, right?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.690
That's being way too harsh!

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.470
But it's spot-on!

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.300
Well, it's true that 
we did save people...

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.170
Well, compared to our 
Gatchaman predecessors,

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.680
we're pathetic enough.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.850
Aw, now my shoulders are tense.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.740
Please keep it together, Leader.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.690
Oh, are you interested?

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:38.780
I'll give this to you, then.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.110
Here!

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.270
I'm gloomy...

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:11.040
That's a troublesome neighbor 
you've got there.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.830
We have a baby, 
so, of course, the baby will cry.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.760
But the neighbor says 
we're being too loud

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.150
and playing music with 
the volume cranked way up...

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.360
They might both be unwanted noise,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.300
but for entirely different reasons.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.840
Things have escalated recently.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.220
Even at night, the neighbor 
honks the car horn.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.810
It's enough to make 
my baby seize up.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.560
Maybe you should 
lodge a complaint.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.630
You mean, take legal action?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.370
But I have no experience 
in that sort of thing...

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.980
Why don't you ask X?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.230
You're right. I will.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.320
What may I help you with?

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.510
May I?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:01.340
Civil lawsuits aren't 
too much trouble.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.180
What?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:03.750
If you'd like,

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.820
Someone's having 
neighbor issues. 
Please help!

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.820
Join            Close

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.840
I can give you counsel.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.460
Are you a lawyer?

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:11.180
Yes. First, tell me what's 
happening, in detail.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.680
It's not heroes who'll 
update the world.
It's us.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.450
Seriously?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:15.570
You're a GALAXTER, too, Marippu?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.700
That sounds like trash (garakuta).

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.210
Hey!

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.250
Fine, fine.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.340
You're asking me if I'm 
a GALAX user, right?

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.660
Of course, I am.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.150
It comes in handy, doesn't it?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.780
GALAX is good stuff.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.460
The info you can get 
from the X app is pretty useful.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.030
Hey, isn't that scary?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.290
There's got to be flame 
wars and stuff, right?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.830
It's all fine.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.850
They're good at managing it.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.210
They match users up in a good way.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:45.780
Just give it a try.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.130
Let's update the world together!

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.790
What's that?

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.930
I'm back.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.320
Welcome back, Rui.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.260
Were you able to secure 
a sufficient caloric intake?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:07.950
Yes.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.150
Update.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.760
A balanced diet is very important.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.520
Good health is essential 
for realizing your ambitions.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.160
Very nice, X.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.830
You've become good 
at managing GALAX, too.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.770
Thank you, Milord Rui.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.130
Hm?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.630
<i>There has been a noticeable</i>

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>decline in job seekers, 
given the lack of economic recovery</i>

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.240
<i>and effective policies 
for the foreseeable feature.</i>

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.730
<i>In actuality, job seekers appear 
to be relying, not on agencies,</i>

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.360
<i>but on GALAX.</i>

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:50.000
Basically, it's a problem of matching 
job seekers with employers.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.530
If they can contact each 
other directly online,

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.530
why would they need a middle man?

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.370
Our active users are 
continuing to increase today.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:04.430
That means the number of people 
who resent us will also increase.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.200
The more powerful the enemy,

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.050
the more enjoyable 
the game, perhaps?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:16.850
Missing Persons Simultaneously Found Across the Nation

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.780
<i>Well, I'm the one who's shocked.</i>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.850
<i>When I came to, I was standing 
on my usual way home,</i>

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.480
<i>but I was told it's been 
more than six months.</i>

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.660
<i>Not just this man,</i>

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.070
<i>but others who had gone missing 
are being found across the country.</i>

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:31.070
<i>They all have no memory 
of the lost time.</i>

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.070
What, what?

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.580
Were they abducted by aliens?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.370
No way.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:46.790
Prime Minister Resigning

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.170
<i>This just in.</i>

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.620
<i>Prime Minister Kamoshida, who had 
been urged to take responsibility</i>

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.830
<i>for his cabinet members' 
multiple scandals,</i>

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.250
<i>indicated his intent to resign today.</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.490
<i>We'll be reporting live from 
the prime minister's residence...</i>

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:54.880
Aww... and this one'd started off 
with high approval ratings, too.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.080
Congratulations, Rui.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.880
Stage clear, isn't it?

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.600
He wasn't really a boss character...

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:08.620
The world's so complicated now 
that even excellent leaders

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.130
might not be enough 
to turn things around.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:14.220
Then, who is the true enemy...

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.870
Who is it? One of the Hundred?

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.890
An incoming call from Number 26.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:24.980
Him...

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.210
It's probably to ask for 
usage permission, I'm sure.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.380
Shall I handle him?

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.660
Sorry, yeah.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.760
What a waste, Rui-Rui.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.470
Are you being stingy with 
that valuable power of yours?

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.170
I did give them power.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.740
the hundred capable GALAXTERs I chose.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.610
But we'll update the world 
without relying on that power.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:55.800
No matter what!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.160
You're going to take 
that thing along to school?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.700
It's fine.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.750
We're the only ones who can see it.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.530
Well, sure, but...

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.390
That was close!

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.890
I wonder if something's happening.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.300
Either way, he shouldn't have 
driven so fast on this road!

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:20.290
But he may have been 
driving a sick person.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.810
Oh, maybe his wife 
went into sudden labor?

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.700
Why do you bother 
thinking about things like that?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.830
When you think about it that way, 
don't you feel like they had a valid reason?

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.440
Don't you feel less angry?

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:34.810
Well, sure...

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.740
It's more fun this way.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:50.760
So, "The current of the 
flowing river does not cease"

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.380
might be a phrase even 
you guys have heard.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:58.590
Kamono Choumei was a court 
poet in his younger years...

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:57.930
Milk?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.960
There has been a worrisome leak.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:04.730
Last night, there was a power outage 
at a factory in Tokorozawa,

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.560
and milk was left at room 
temperature for several hours.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.310
Class is finished!

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:15.240
According to the source,

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.780
even though disposal 
was recommended,

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.790
the supervisor would not allow it.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.110
Instead, the batch was 
shipped out after undergoing

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.040
a simple disinfection procedure.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:26.440
Is that bad?

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.380
Yes.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.800
There were factors indicating 
a potential emergency situation,

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.000
so I illegally obtained data 
on the batch's management

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.220
and component analysis, 
and ran an analysis.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:38.210
So you did some cracking?

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.970
Well, I guess it couldn't be helped.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.050
So, are they guilty?

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.350
Thanks for the food!

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.270
Yep, looking good.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.550
Yummy!

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.150
Milk?

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:02.740
Wait a minute.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.300
Thanks for the food.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.010
It's from X.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.440
The milk's not safe!

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.910
Huh? What?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.940
What's wrong with it?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:10.950
It's urgent, Senpai!

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:13.460
C'mon! Help us out!

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.830
We got to the kiosk lady okay.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.890
Next, a school-wide announcement 
and then hit the vending machines.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.930
Yeah! Split up and unplug them!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.330
Wait a minute.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.090
Did you get permission 
from the teachers?

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.830
There's no time for that!

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.490
Have you heard about the milk?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.680
Please tell the others!

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.110
I feel gloomy...

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.410
Seriously?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.410
It's an anti-tampering device.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:55.210
Oh, no announcement yet?

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.280
They won't let us in.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:00.460
The broadcast room is only 
accessible from the teachers' lounge.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:03.140
So, we need to tell everyone!

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.200
Isn't it a ruse?

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.470
We can't just take stuff 
from the internet at face value.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:11.580
But there are lots of people 
who've been helped by GALAX.

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.810
Yeah, X tells us everything, too.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:18.680
You'd better not be using it to cheat.

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.750
Oh, c'mon! That's not why we're here!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.280
Um...

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:23.860
I'm using GALAX, too,

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.230
and I think it can be trusted...

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.140
Maybe we can, 
at least, urge caution...

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.410
Anyway, we should 
consult the principal.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.260
Consult?

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:33.830
That'll be too late.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.110
Where's the key 
to the vending machines?

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:36.430
That's also in the teachers' lounge.

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:38.080
They say we need permission...

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.430
I'll send a decoy. 
Let's use this opportunity.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:43.710
Oh, it's kind of like a game.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:44.920
A decoy?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.520
You, of course, Senpai.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.500
Use your sword and mess around.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.270
Huh, what?!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.930
You can use an umbrella 
or whatever, too.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:53.670
Get the attention 
of people who are getting

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.120
in the way at the teachers' lounge
and in front of the broadcast room.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.390
That's impossible!

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.270
Besides, what about 
my reputation at school?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.360
Senpai, you're a Gatchaman, right?

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.530
N-Not so loud!

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.800
The school's in a crisis.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:10.180
But that's no excuse to skulk 
around and go out of control!

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.370
Heroes should face 
problems head-on.

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:14.200
Listen, Senpai.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.160
It's like that car 
earlier this morning.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:19.420
That car wasn't 
out of control for no reason.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.810
Well, you don't know 
if there really was a reason.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.610
That's just your speculation.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.050
But now, we definitely have a reason.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:29.490
You're a hero, right, Senpai?

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:32.970
We have to protect everyone!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.180
Where's the key?

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.440
O-Over there.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:43.940
The key to the vending machines
is probably there, too.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.000
Don't drink the milk!

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:05.930
Okay!

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:06.750
Next!

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.880
Are you still using the key?

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.650
They're in front of the 
inner courtyard now.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.110
Oh, they're done.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:16.950
This one's the last of them!

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.470
What now? Should we go get it?

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.310
Oh, Senpai!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.770
Can you slash right here?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.730
Slash?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:25.980
Slash!

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.430
Fine!

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.690
Here goes!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.990
I slashed it!

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:39.970
Congratulations!

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:43.170
The world has been updated.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.920
Mission complete.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:48.050
Yay, updated!

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:57.230
Nationwide, 68% percent of schools

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:59.280
and 74% of businesses 
averted any casualties.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:06.020
Flaw in Quality Control at Dairy Company

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:02.730
Victims who made purchases 
from individual stores

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.020
and wholesale distributors 
number in the double digits.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.150
That's more than I thought.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.640
Is that an indication 
of just how many

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.480
people still don't trust 
information from GALAX?

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.560
It is true that people 
of a certain age range

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:20.370
or in certain professions 
exhibit markedly lower confidence.

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:24.060
However, many who 
acknowledged the information

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.460
were still unable to take 
appropriate action.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.340
Oh, I see.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:33.400
They're afraid of being held 
responsible in the aftermath,

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.640
so they cannot easily take action 
based on outside information.

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:40.160
It's what people call the adverse 
effects of a vertical society.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.660
That's probably what we're 
actually up against.

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:50.070
Running GALAX has made 
my enemies clearer than ever to me.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.870
They're the ones who refuse 
to see people as individuals.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:56.080
The ones who cannot see the joy

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:59.610
in helping others if there is no 
reward or reputation to be gained.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.580
Either way,

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.870
anyone who's not... fun, I guess?

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.970
Oh, that was great, Senpai.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:16.090
You looked kind of cute 
being scolded by the teachers.

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.510
Is that your attempt 
to make me feel better?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.470
Oh, you wanted me to do that?

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:22.490
What are you doing?

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:25.750
But, well...

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:30.120
This kind of... the internet's 
got a lot going for it, maybe.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.870
You think so?

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.820
Its influence is huge.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.600
That's not true.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.410
Huh?

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.950
If your battery runs out, 
or if you don't have a signal, that's it.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:44.150
You can't just blindly 
follow the internet.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:45.460
Okay, then.

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:57.300
Hey, stop it, Al-chan.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.010
Stop. It tickles.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.660
It's dinner time!

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.510
Come help.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:05.640
Okay.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.910
Wait a second, okay?

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.920
Oh?

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.430
Oh...

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.970
Is that from Hajime-chan?

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.060
She just pushed it on me.

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.660
That girl's way too fun!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.510
Why don't you become friends?

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:33.880
Here.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:40.000
All right, beans are 
on the menu today.

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:42.990
I'm gloomy...

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.270
Can you circle around 
and get closer?

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.250
I want the setting sun 
in the background.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.530
Multiple rescue requests 
have appeared on the timeline.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:03.510
A news channel helicopter has crashed 
into a ropeway's support pillar.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:07.370
The pillars bent, stranding 
the two gondolas on either side.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.960
You brought that to school?

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.960
Isn't Toyosaki, 
the gym teacher, annoying?

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.350
That doesn't mean you should—

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:18.920
Well, it's not like I'm going 
to do anything to him with it.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.580
What?

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:57.130
Now!

00:19:58.470 --> 00:19:59.210
You!

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:00.720
Stop resisting!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:01.740
Don't move!

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.400
What?

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.470
Where is he? Where'd he go?

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:09.930
Look around!

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:12.510
Hey, there he is!

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.440
N-No!

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.380
Stop resisting!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.380
It wasn't me!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.570
L-Let go of me!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:17.610
Let go!

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.190
Gatcha...

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.580
Who are you?

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:31.810
Was that your doing?

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:35.830
Yummy...

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:37.840
Go...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:45.560
Number 58 of the Hundred 
is on the dispatched rescue team.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.230
They are in operation,

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.310
but due to numerous obstacles 
that cannot be overcome,

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.530
he is requesting usage permission.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.210
There are several GALAXTERs among

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.390
the passengers exchanging information,

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.360
but the situation seems pretty dire.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:20:59.980
I see...

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:05.010
If we don't use <i>it</i> now, when else?

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.370
The rescue team alone would 
just end in a fail game.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.620
I simulated all possible avenues 
for a successful rescue

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.830
given the current available 
human resources,

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.560
but all results were negative.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:19.750
I guess we'll have to use...
the Crowds.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.020
Ready!

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.530
Play the Game...
